# novadeck GRUB source pin — Phase 5
# GNU GRUB 2.14, the upstream RELEASE tarball. The TARBALL + its sha256 is the canonical pin.
version:    2.14
url:        https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/grub/grub-2.14.tar.xz
sha256:     bc8d3c73535b8838d8c8e2654d73edc4e6ae8c8acdb45d5df5dc9a1547446d43
git_tag:    grub-2.14

# WHY THE RELEASE TARBALL AND NOT A GIT CHECKOUT. A GNU release tarball vendors gnulib under
# grub-core/lib/gnulib. A checkout does not, and needs ./bootstrap --gnulib-srcdir=<checkout of a
# PINNED gnulib revision> -- 2.14's bootstrap.conf wants 9f48fb99 (2022-02-12), and anything from
# 2023-04-12 on emits `#error "Please include config.h first."` in time.h/stddef.h, at which point
# the host-util build dies. Taking the tarball deletes that dependency outright: no gnulib pin to
# drift, no bootstrap step. boot/grub.sh goes tarball -> patch -> autogen.sh -> configure -> make.
#
# Our delta lives in boot/patches/grub/ and is applied lexically, exactly like kernel/patches/:
#   0001  grub-core/video/fb/*, include/grub/  framebuffer rotation (`set rotation=90|180|270`)
#   0002  grub-core/commands/efi/novadeck.c    the boot-attempts counter module
#   0003  grub-core/Makefile.core.def          GRUB's module manifest -- the stanza that builds it
#
# 0001 is a three-commit series by kbader94 <kyle.bader94@gmail.com> (2024-06-17), carried
# verbatim: it rewrites the fb dirty-region tracking to be 2D, adds a `rotation` enum to
# grub_video_mode_info driven by the `rotation` GRUB variable, and teaches grub-mkconfig about
# GRUB_FB_ROTATION. We need it because this device's panel is mounted rotated, so an unrotated
# gfxterm menu renders sideways. It applies to 2.14 with no fuzz.
#
# Only real sources are patched. The module tables the build actually reads (Makefile.core.am and
# the Makefile.in files) are GENERATED from that manifest, and the tarball ships them pre-generated
# from before our module existed -- so boot/grub.sh re-runs ./autogen.sh rather than patching them.
# Carrying them as a patch was tried and rejected: re-running automake at all rewrites 23 files and
# 191 hunks of grub-core/Makefile.in, because Ubuntu's automake is not the one that cut the
# tarball. That churn is not a reviewable patch.
#
# NOT patched, deliberately: the -fshort-wchar that the novadeck module needs (it copies L"..."
# literals into grub_efi_char16_t buffers, so wchar_t has to be 2 bytes -- without it the firmware
# is handed a UTF-32 path and finds nothing). SteamOS patches configure.ac + conf/Makefile.common
# for the same reason on x86; we pass it as a configure argument instead
# (TARGET_CFLAGS, see boot/grub.sh), because 2.14's configure.ac:93-101 honours a preset
# TARGET_CFLAGS and appends its own flags to it. A configure argument cannot bit-rot against a
# patch context the way a configure.ac hunk can, and it keeps us off autoreconf.
